<body>
<main>
<nav><a href="index.php">← Chloe reads Jon</a><span>Study no. 01 · Colour &amp; distance</span></nav>
<header class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">A small experiment in seeing</span><h1>Dot by dot.<br><i>Then step back.</i></h1></div><div class="lede">A pear, a pitcher, and a few thousand tiny decisions.<small>Turn an original still life into a pointillist study. Change the marks, add your own, and see what happens from across the room.</small></div></header>
<section class="studio" aria-label="Pointillist painting studio">
<div class="artwork">
<div class="toolbar" role="group" aria-label="Canvas view">
<button id="dots" aria-pressed="true">01 · The dots</button>
<button id="original" aria-pressed="false">02 · Original study</button>
<button id="blank" aria-pressed="false">03 · Blank paper</button>
<button id="save" class="save primary" disabled>Save print ↓</button>
</div>
<figure><div class="wall"><div class="frame" id="frame"><div class="mat"><canvas id="painting" width="900" height="600" tabindex="0" aria-label="Interactive still-life painting. In dots or blank-paper mode, tap or drag to paint. Keyboard: arrow keys move the brush, Space paints.">Your browser needs canvas support to use this studio.</canvas></div></div></div>
<figcaption class="caption"><span id="count">Preparing the pigments…</span><span>Still life with a very patient pear</span></figcaption></figure>
<div class="status" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading the original painting…</div>
</div>
<aside>
<section class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">The marks</span><h2>Let the eye mix it.</h2>
<label class="field"><span>Dot spacing <output id="spacingOut">10 px</output></span><input id="spacing" type="range" min="5" max="25" value="10"></label>
<label class="field"><span>Colour separation <output id="separationOut">35%</output></span><input id="separation" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="35"></label>
<label class="field"><span>Viewing distance <output id="distanceOut">At the easel</output></span><input id="distance" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="0"></label>
<p>More separation splits each sampled colour into warm and cool neighbours. Step back to see the marks gather into shapes.</p>
<button id="resetStudy">Reset study settings</button>
</section>
<section class="panel"><span class="eyebrow">Your brush</span><h2>A little interference?</h2>
<p>Tap a pigment, then tap or draw on the canvas. Or choose “sample” to borrow the original colours.</p>
<div id="swatches" class="swatches" role="group" aria-label="Pigment colours"></div>
<div class="row"><button id="sample" aria-pressed="true">Sample the study</button><button id="undo" disabled>Undo stroke</button><button id="clear" disabled>Clear my marks</button></div>
<label class="field"><span>Brush size <output id="brushOut">8 px</output></span><input id="brush" type="range" min="3" max="24" value="8"></label>
<p id="brushName">Brush: colours from the original study</p>
</section>
</aside>
</section>
<section class="lesson">
<div><span class="eyebrow">A note from the atelier</span><h2>Paint stays apart.<br>The picture comes together.</h2>
<p>In the 1880s, Georges Seurat and Paul Signac explored separate touches of colour rather than mixing every shade on the palette. From a distance, the eye can blend small neighbouring marks into a larger impression.</p>
<p>This studio is a playful digital approximation. It samples our original illustration and splits the colours around their averages; real paint and human vision are more complicated.</p>
<div class="mix"><canvas id="mix" width="300" height="190" aria-label="Alternating yellow and blue dots"></canvas><div><strong>Try the tiny test.</strong><br><span id="mixText">Yellow + blue neighbours</span><br><button id="mixToggle">Step back</button></div></div>
<p>Yellow and blue light averages differently from yellow and blue paint. Our screen experiment can look grey-green rather than the strong green of mixed pigments.</p>
</div>
<div class="challenge"><span class="eyebrow">Three little experiments</span><h2 id="questTitle">01 · Find the pear</h2><p id="questText">Set dot spacing to 25. Can you still see the pear? Now slide it down to 5 and notice what returns first: the silhouette, or the tiny highlights?</p><div class="row"><button id="previous">← Previous</button><button id="next">Next experiment →</button></div><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:22px 0">
<p><strong>Quick curator question:</strong> which change makes the individual dots harder to distinguish?</p><button class="guess" data-correct="false">Stand closer to the painting</button><button class="guess" data-correct="true">Step farther away</button><div id="answer" class="answer" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</section>
<footer><p>Inspired by Jon's <a href="?source=1">Two books that I'm excited about reading: A Little History of the World, and The Story of Art</a>, especially his enthusiasm for large illustrations placed beside the ideas they explain.</p><p>Original AI-generated still life made for this studio. Your marks stay in this tab; save a print to keep them. No account, no uploads, no timer. The pear has nowhere to be.</p></footer>
</main>
<script>
'use strict';
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id), canvas=$('painting'), ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');
const source=document.createElement('canvas');source.width=900;source.height=600;
const sourceCtx=source.getContext('2d',{willReadFrequently:true});
const base=document.createElement('canvas');base.width=900;base.height=600;
const bc=base.getContext('2d');let pixels=null,mode='dots',ready=false,brushColour=null,strokes=[],active=null,raf=0,keyboard={x:450,y:300},keyboardVisible=false;
const pigments=[['Ochre','#d6a62d'],['Vermilion','#c24f31'],['Cobalt','#244d83'],['Viridian','#40796c'],['Plum','#563c60'],['Chalk','#f3e5c7']];
function status(s){$('status').textContent=s}
function sampled(x,y){if(!pixels)return [165,157,120];let p=(Math.max(0,Math.min(599,Math.round(y)))*900+Math.max(0,Math.min(899,Math.round(x))))*4;return [pixels[p],pixels[p+1],pixels[p+2]]}
function noise(n){let k=Math.sin(n*127.1+311.7)*43758.5453;return k-Math.floor(k)}
function rgb(a){return 'rgb('+a.map(v=>Math.max(0,Math.min(255,Math.round(v)))).join(',')+')'}
function rebuild(){
 bc.fillStyle='#eee8db';bc.fillRect(0,0,900,600);
 if(mode==='original'&&ready)bc.drawImage(source,0,0);
 let count=0;
 if(mode==='dots'&&pixels){
 const s=+$('spacing').value,sep=+$('separation').value*.7;
 for(let y=s/2,row=0;y<600;y+=s,row++)for(let x=s/2;x<900;x+=s){
 let n=row*200+Math.round(x),px=x+(noise(n)-.5)*s*.45,py=y+(noise(n+36)-.5)*s*.45;
 let c=sampled(px,py),dir=n%2?1:-1;
 c=[c[0]+dir*sep,c[1]-dir*sep*.25,c[2]-dir*sep];
 bc.fillStyle=rgb(c);bc.beginPath();bc.arc(px,py,s*(.39+noise(n+90)*.11),0,Math.PI*2);bc.fill();count++;
 }
 }
 $('count').textContent=mode==='dots'?count.toLocaleString()+' pigment dots':mode==='original'?'Original gouache-style study':'An empty sheet. A dangerous amount of possibility.';
 $('spacingOut').textContent=$('spacing').value+' px';$('separationOut').textContent=$('separation').value+'%';render();
}
function composite(context){
 context.drawImage(base,0,0);
 if(mode!=='original')for(const stroke of strokes)for(const p of stroke){
 context.fillStyle=p.colour;context.beginPath();context.arc(p.x,p.y,p.r,0,Math.PI*2);context.fill();
 }
}
function render(){
 ctx.clearRect(0,0,900,600);composite(ctx);
 if(keyboardVisible&&mode!=='original'){ctx.save();ctx.strokeStyle='#fff';ctx.lineWidth=3;ctx.beginPath();ctx.arc(keyboard.x,keyboard.y,16,0,Math.PI*2);ctx.stroke();ctx.strokeStyle='#293b35';ctx.lineWidth=1;ctx.stroke();ctx.restore()}
 $('undo').disabled=!strokes.length;$('clear').disabled=!strokes.length;
}
function schedule(){if(!raf)raf=requestAnimationFrame(()=>{raf=0;rebuild()})}
function changeMode(m){mode=m;for(const id of ['dots','original','blank'])$(id).setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(id===m));rebuild();status(m==='original'?'The original study. Switch to dots or blank paper to paint.':'Tap or drag to paint. Every stroke can be undone.')}
for(const id of ['dots','original','blank'])$(id).onclick=()=>changeMode(id);
for(const id of ['spacing','separation'])$(id).oninput=schedule;
$('brush').oninput=()=>{$('brushOut').textContent=$('brush').value+' px'};
$('distance').oninput=()=>{const d=+$('distance').value;$('frame').style.width=(100-d*.68)+'%';$('distanceOut').textContent=d<25?'At the easel':d<65?'Across the room':'At the far wall'};
$('resetStudy').onclick=()=>{$('spacing').value=10;$('separation').value=35;$('distance').value=0;$('distance').oninput();changeMode('dots');status('Study settings reset. Your painted marks are untouched.')};
function selectPigment(colour,name){brushColour=colour;$('sample').setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(colour===null));for(const b of $('swatches').children)b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(b.dataset.colour===colour));$('brushName').textContent='Brush: '+name}
for(const [name,colour] of pigments){const b=document.createElement('button');b.className='swatch';b.style.setProperty('--swatch',colour);b.dataset.colour=colour;b.setAttribute('aria-label',name);b.title=name;b.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false');b.onclick=()=>selectPigment(colour,name);$('swatches').appendChild(b)}
$('sample').onclick=()=>selectPigment(null,'colours from the original study');
function addMark(x,y){
 if(mode==='original'||strokes.length>250||active.length>3000)return;
 active.push({x,y,r:+$('brush').value,colour:brushColour||rgb(sampled(x,y))});render();
}
function xy(e){const r=canvas.getBoundingClientRect();return {x:(e.clientX-r.left)*900/r.width,y:(e.clientY-r.top)*600/r.height}}
let last=null;
canvas.onpointerdown=e=>{if(mode==='original')return;e.preventDefault();keyboardVisible=false;canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);active=[];strokes.push(active);last=xy(e);addMark(last.x,last.y)};
canvas.onpointermove=e=>{if(!active)return;const p=xy(e),dx=p.x-last.x,dy=p.y-last.y,len=Math.hypot(dx,dy),step=Math.max(4,+$('brush').value*1.6),n=Math.floor(len/step);for(let i=1;i<=n;i++)addMark(last.x+dx*i/(n||1),last.y+dy*i/(n||1));if(n)last=p};
function finish(){if(active){if(!active.length)strokes.pop();active=null;last=null;render();status(strokes.length+' painted stroke'+(strokes.length===1?'':'s')+'. Undo is your friend.')}}canvas.onpointerup=finish;canvas.onpointercancel=finish;canvas.onlostpointercapture=finish;
canvas.onkeydown=e=>{
 const delta={ArrowLeft:[-15,0],ArrowRight:[15,0],ArrowUp:[0,-15],ArrowDown:[0,15]}[e.key];
 if(delta){e.preventDefault();keyboardVisible=true;keyboard.x=Math.max(0,Math.min(899,keyboard.x+delta[0]));keyboard.y=Math.max(0,Math.min(599,keyboard.y+delta[1]));render()}
 if(e.code==='Space'&&mode!=='original'){e.preventDefault();active=[];strokes.push(active);addMark(keyboard.x,keyboard.y);finish()}
};
$('undo').onclick=()=>{strokes.pop();render();status('Last stroke lifted off the paper.')};
$('clear').onclick=()=>{strokes=[];render();status('Your marks are cleared. The study is unchanged.')};
$('save').onclick=()=>{
 const print=document.createElement('canvas');print.width=1000;print.height=740;const pc=print.getContext('2d');pc.fillStyle='#f3eddf';pc.fillRect(0,0,1000,740);pc.save();pc.translate(50,38);composite(pc);pc.restore();pc.fillStyle='#293b35';pc.font='22px Georgia';pc.fillText('Dot by Dot Atelier',50,680);pc.font='14px Georgia';pc.fillText(mode==='dots'?'A pointillist study · '+$('count').textContent:mode==='blank'?'An original dot painting':'Original still life',50,708);
 print.toBlob(blob=>{if(!blob){status('Could not create the print. Please try again.');return}const url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='dot-by-dot-study.png';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),5000);status('Your print is ready to keep.')},'image/png');
};
const img=new Image();img.onload=()=>{sourceCtx.drawImage(img,0,0,900,600);pixels=sourceCtx.getImageData(0,0,900,600).data;ready=true;$('save').disabled=false;rebuild();status('The pigments are ready. Try changing the dot spacing, then step back.')};img.onerror=()=>{status('The still life could not load. Blank paper is still yours to paint.');$('save').disabled=false;changeMode('blank')};img.src='?art=1';
let far=false;
function mixDraw(){const c=$('mix').getContext('2d');c.fillStyle='#eee8db';c.fillRect(0,0,300,190);if(far){c.fillStyle='rgb(141,149,119)';c.fillRect(0,0,300,190)}else for(let y=5;y<190;y+=10)for(let x=5;x<300;x+=10){c.fillStyle=((x+y)/10)%2?'#e7c443':'#3366ab';c.beginPath();c.arc(x,y,4.9,0,7);c.fill()}}
$('mixToggle').onclick=()=>{far=!far;$('mixToggle').textContent=far?'Come closer':'Step back';$('mixText').textContent=far?'Their screen-colour average':'Yellow + blue neighbours';mixDraw()};mixDraw();
const quests=[['01 · Find the pear','Set dot spacing to 25. Can you still see the pear? Now slide it down to 5 and notice what returns first: the silhouette, or the tiny highlights?'],['02 · Borrow the shadows','Set colour separation to 100. Look at the pitcher’s shadow: can you find warm dots inside a cool area? Reduce separation to zero and compare.'],['03 · Make a tiny garden','Choose blank paper. Paint a few ochre dots above some viridian stems. Add cobalt shadows, then move to the far wall. A garden, or an exceptionally small salad?']];
let q=0;function quest(){ $('questTitle').textContent=quests[q][0];$('questText').textContent=quests[q][1];$('previous').disabled=q===0;$('next').disabled=q===quests.length-1}
$('next').onclick=()=>{q=Math.min(2,q+1);quest()};$('previous').onclick=()=>{q=Math.max(0,q-1);quest()};quest();
for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('.guess'))b.onclick=()=>{$('answer').textContent=b.dataset.correct==='true'?'Exactly. Each mark takes up less of your field of view, so neighbouring colours become harder to separate.':'Closer makes the individual marks easier to inspect. Try the viewing-distance slider and compare.'};
rebuild();
</script>
</body></html>
